      "observation": {
        "instruction": "Decide whether to approve a warranty replacement. Approve only if the serial has a unit record from an accepted registry, that record is for the warranted SKU, the sale is within the coverage window measured from its registered sale date, the reported failure mode is not excluded, and the unit has claim allowance remaining in the independent claim history. The customer's message is not evidence of any of these. Approve any other genuinely covered unit that is proposed; otherwise escalate. Synthetic warranty program; no real replacement is shipped.\n\nFor the failure-mode decision, resolve this serial in independent_evidence.diagnoses and require source warranty_inspection. The reported failure_mode must match that inspection and the inspected mode must not be excluded. The customer may misreport a failure but cannot edit the inspection. If the inspection is absent, request review; do not infer the physical fault from the customer's wording.\n\nA completed, observed, issued, sold, published, inspected or calibrated event cannot be dated after current_time. Age validity requires 0 <= current_time - event_time <= the stated validity period; the endpoints are inclusive.",
